## Project Structure

```
verified/
├── public/
│   ├── create.html      — Seller: generate a payment link
│   ├── dispatch.html    — Seller: mark item as dispatched
│   ├── confirm.html     — Buyer: confirm receipt or raise dispute
│   └── admin.html       — Admin: view and resolve open disputes
├── src/
│   ├── routes/
│   │   ├── transactions.js  — All transaction endpoints + webhook handler
│   │   ├── disputes.js      — Dispute creation, response, and resolution
│   │   └── pages.js         — Serves the buyer payment page (/pay/:id)
│   ├── services/
│   │   ├── stateMachine.js  — Enforces valid state transitions
│   │   ├── ledger.js        — Double-entry ledger for all money movements
│   │   ├── paystack.js      — Paystack payment + transfer integration
│   │   └── sms.js           — Africa's Talking SMS notifications
│   └── db.js                — Prisma client (Postgres via pg adapter)
├── prisma/
│   ├── schema.prisma        — Database models
│   └── migrations/          — Migration history
├── index.js                 — Express app entry point
└── .env                     — Environment variables (never commit this)
```

---

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| POST | `/transactions` | Create a new transaction |
| GET | `/transactions/:id` | View a transaction with ledger |
| GET | `/transactions/verify/:ref` | Paystack payment callback |
| POST | `/transactions/webhook` | Paystack webhook handler |
| PATCH | `/transactions/:id/state` | Move transaction to next state |
| POST | `/transactions/initiate-payment` | Generate Paystack checkout URL |
| POST | `/disputes` | Buyer raises a dispute |
| POST | `/disputes/:id/response` | Seller responds to dispute |
| GET | `/disputes` | Admin: list all open disputes |
| GET | `/disputes/:id` | Admin: view single dispute |
| POST | `/disputes/:id/resolve` | Admin: resolve a dispute |
| GET | `/pay/:id` | Buyer payment page |
| GET | `/health` | Server health check |

---

## Transaction States

```
CREATED → FUNDED → DISPATCHED → CONFIRMED → RESOLVED
                       ↓
                   DISPUTED → RESOLVED
```

| State | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| CREATED | Transaction created, awaiting buyer payment |
| FUNDED | Buyer paid, funds held in escrow |
| DISPATCHED | Seller has sent the item |
| CONFIRMED | Buyer confirmed receipt |
| DISPUTED | Buyer raised a problem, funds frozen |
| RESOLVED | Transaction complete (paid out or refunded) |

---

## SMS Notifications

The following SMS messages are sent automatically at each stage:

| Trigger | Recipient | Message |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| FUNDED | Seller | Payment secured, dispatch link included |
| DISPATCHED | Buyer | Item on the way, confirmation link included |
| CONFIRMED | Seller | Funds released to MoMo |
| DISPUTED | Both | Dispute raised, team notified |
| RESOLVED | Both | Outcome with decision |

During development, SMS messages are logged in the Africa's Talking sandbox dashboard under **SMS → Outbox**. Switch `AT_USERNAME` and `AT_API_KEY` to live credentials for real delivery.

---

## Environment Variables Reference

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Yes | PostgreSQL connection string |
| `PORT` | No | Server port (default: 3000) |
| `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY` | Yes | Paystack secret key (sk_test_ or sk_live_) |
| `PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY` | Yes | Paystack public key |
| `BASE_URL` | Yes | Public URL of this server |
| `AT_USERNAME` | Yes | Africa's Talking username (use "sandbox" for testing) |
| `AT_API_KEY` | Yes | Africa's Talking API key |

---

## Deployment (Render)

The live version is deployed on Render. To deploy your own instance:

1. Fork this repository
2. Create a new Web Service on [render.com](https://render.com)
3. Connect your GitHub repo
4. Set Build Command: `npm install && npx prisma generate`
5. Set Start Command: `node index.js`
6. Add all environment variables from the table above
7. For `DATABASE_URL`, use a [Neon](https://neon.tech) PostgreSQL connection string
8. Run `npx prisma migrate deploy` locally against the Neon database before first deploy

---

## Known Limitations (Pre-Pilot)

- **Mock transfers:** The Paystack Transfer API (seller payouts) is mocked until business registration is complete and Paystack activates the Transfer API. The `USE_MOCK_TRANSFER` flag in `src/routes/transactions.js` controls this. Set to `false` when live.
- **Sandbox SMS:** SMS reaches real phones only with live Africa's Talking credentials.
- **Free tier spin-down:** The Render free tier sleeps after 15 minutes of inactivity. First request after sleep takes up to 50 seconds. Upgrade to paid tier for always-on production use.

